<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 23 November, from 1248 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/seville" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seville.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1248 CE <span class="tih-ago">778 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Seville surrenders to Ferdinand III of Castile</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of more than a year, the Muslim city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III of Castile</a>. Its fall left the Nasrid kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> as the main surviving Muslim state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III of Castile</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1499 CE <span class="tih-ago">527 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The pretender Perkin Warbeck is hanged at Tyburn</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Perkin Warbeck, who had claimed to be Richard, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>, the younger of the 'Princes in the Tower', was hanged after a failed escape. His death removed a persistent threat to Henry VII.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1644 CE <span class="tih-ago">382 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Milton publishes Areopagitica</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Milton issued Areopagitica, an unlicensed pamphlet arguing against Parliament's censorship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a>. It became a classic defence of freedom of the press.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1889 CE <span class="tih-ago">137 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first coin-operated phonograph plays in San Francisco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Louis <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gla">Glass</a> installed a coin-in-the-slot phonograph at the Palais Royale Saloon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a>. Listening through tubes, customers paid a nickel a song, the ancestor of the jukebox.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1963 CE <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Doctor Who is first broadcast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The BBC broadcast the first episode of Doctor Who, about a time-travelling alien in a police box. It became the longest-running science fiction television series in the world.</p></div></li></ol>
